IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `taa-review-penalties`

-- Taxation Administration Act 1953, Part IVC, Schedule 1 Divisions 284, 286, 298 and Subdivision 426-D -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_taxation-administration-act-1953_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*): Chloe turns 15 on 14 March 2018 and takes a casual job
-- at a supermarket (c020); her first graduate payslip on 29 February 2024 is $5,833.33 for the month (c041). Daniel turns 16 on
-- 15 October 2012 with a TFN and a casual job (d012). Jake turns 15 on 30 August 2021 with a TFN and no job (k020); on 20 October
-- 2028 he lodges his first return as a sole trader on $31,000, not registered for GST (k043). Daniel founds the Rossi
-- Foundation, a private ancillary fund, on 1 March 2051 and gives it $2,000,000 (d072); on 3 May 2076 its trustee company passes
-- to his children (d091).
-- Figures the scenarios do not give are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL, and labelled where used. The text encoded is the 2026
-- compilation, not the law as it stood in 2012 or 2018, or as it will stand in 2051 or 2076.

-- k043 assumptions, HYPOTHETICAL: notice of Jake's 2028-29 assessment given 15 November 2029, and the 2-year period of review
-- applies to him (ITAA 1936 s 170(1) -- a borrowed fact); a penalty notice of 1 March 2030; a return due 31 October 2029; a penalty
-- unit of $330 (the Crimes Act figure before indexation). d091: a notice removing the trustee served 1 June 2076 (HYPOTHETICAL).

`k043: Jake objects to his 2028-29 assessment` MEANS `My objection` WITH
    `what I object to` IS `my income tax assessment`
    `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS (Date 15 11 2029)
    `the day I was given notice of my income tax assessment` IS (Date 15 11 2029)
    `the 2-year period of review applies to my assessment` IS TRUE

`k043: Jake objects to a shortfall penalty on that assessment` MEANS `My objection` WITH
    `what I object to` IS `a Division 284 penalty relating to my income tax assessment`
    `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS (Date 1 3 2030)
    `the day I was given notice of my income tax assessment` IS (Date 15 11 2029)
    `the 2-year period of review applies to my assessment` IS TRUE

`d091: the Foundation's trustee company objects to its removal` MEANS `My objection` WITH
    `what I object to` IS `another taxation decision`
    `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS (Date 1 6 2076)
    `the day I was given notice of my income tax assessment` IS (Date 1 6 2076)
    `the 2-year period of review applies to my assessment` IS FALSE

`k043: Jake overstates a deduction in his own return, carelessly` MEANS `My statement` WITH
    `it is false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE
    `my agent and I took reasonable care` IS FALSE
    `a registered tax agent made it for me` IS FALSE
    `I gave the agent all relevant taxation information` IS FALSE
    `the agent was intentionally disregardful or reckless` IS FALSE

`a wrong figure despite reasonable care` MEANS `My statement` WITH
    `it is false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE
    `my agent and I took reasonable care` IS TRUE
    `a registered tax agent made it for me` IS FALSE
    `I gave the agent all relevant taxation information` IS FALSE
    `the agent was intentionally disregardful or reckless` IS FALSE

`Jake tells the Commissioner before any examination` MEANS `What I did about it` WITH
    `I obstructed the Commissioner or did not tell in reasonable time` IS FALSE
    `I had a base penalty under the same items before` IS FALSE
    `I told the Commissioner voluntarily before an examination was notified` IS TRUE
    `I told the Commissioner after an examination was notified, saving significant time` IS FALSE

`Jake hides the shortfall` MEANS `What I did about it` WITH
    `I obstructed the Commissioner or did not tell in reasonable time` IS TRUE
    `I had a base penalty under the same items before` IS FALSE
    `I told the Commissioner voluntarily before an examination was notified` IS FALSE
    `I told the Commissioner after an examination was notified, saving significant time` IS FALSE

`d072: Daniel, a director, knew the Foundation was held out as a DGR after its endorsement lapsed` MEANS `The holding out and my part in it` WITH
    `the trustee held the fund out as a deductible gift recipient` IS TRUE
    `the fund was so endorsed or entitled` IS FALSE
    `the penalty cannot reasonably be recovered from the trustee company` IS TRUE
    `the trustee company is a licensed trustee company or a Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `I was unaware, and could not reasonably have been aware, of the holding out` IS FALSE
    `I took all reasonable steps to stop it` IS FALSE
    `there were no steps I could have taken` IS FALSE

`d091: Anjali, a new director, could not have known of the holding out` MEANS `The holding out and my part in it` WITH
    `the trustee held the fund out as a deductible gift recipient` IS TRUE
    `the fund was so endorsed or entitled` IS FALSE
    `the penalty cannot reasonably be recovered from the trustee company` IS TRUE
    `the trustee company is a licensed trustee company or a Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `I was unaware, and could not reasonably have been aware, of the holding out` IS TRUE
    `I took all reasonable steps to stop it` IS FALSE
    `there were no steps I could have taken` IS FALSE

§ `s 14ZW`

-- k043: 2 years from 15 November 2029 = 15 November 2031. A penalty relating to that assessment takes the same longer period.
-- d091: a removal decision under s 426-125 is objected to under Part IVC within 60 days: 31 July 2076.
#ASSERT `By when must I object` `k043: Jake objects to his 2028-29 assessment` EQUALS (Date 15 11 2031)
#ASSERT `By when must I object` `k043: Jake objects to a shortfall penalty on that assessment` EQUALS (Date 15 11 2031)
#ASSERT `By when must I object` `d091: the Foundation's trustee company objects to its removal` EQUALS (Date 31 7 2076)

§ `ss 14ZW(2), 14ZX`

-- Lodged late with a written request the Commissioner agrees to: treated as in time.
#ASSERT `Is my objection in time` (Date 1 12 2031) (Date 15 11 2031) TRUE TRUE

§ `s 14ZYA`

-- Lodged 10 January 2030, no information asked: the 60 days end on 11 March 2030. Notice requiring a decision given 1 April
-- 2030: taken to be disallowed on 31 May 2030.
#ASSERT `When may I require a decision on my objection` (Date 10 1 2030) (Date 10 1 2030) FALSE (Date 10 1 2030) EQUALS (Date 11 3 2030)

#ASSERT `When is my objection taken to be disallowed` (Date 1 4 2030) EQUALS (Date 31 5 2030)

§ `ss 14ZZ, 14ZZC, 14ZZM, 14ZZN`

-- Served with the objection decision on 15 June 2030: 60 days, to 14 August 2030.
#ASSERT `May I go to the ART` FALSE

#ASSERT `By when must I seek review or appeal` (Date 15 6 2030) EQUALS (Date 14 8 2030)

-- k043: Jake is a small business entity; without an ART stay order the tax can still be recovered while review is pending.
#ASSERT `Can the tax be recovered from me meanwhile` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 284-75`

#ASSERT `Am I liable for a false or misleading statement` `k043: Jake overstates a deduction in his own return, carelessly`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I liable for a false or misleading statement` `a wrong figure despite reasonable care`

§ `ss 284-90, 284-85, 284-220, 284-225`

-- k043, HYPOTHETICAL shortfall of 4,000 from a failure to take reasonable care: 25% = 1,000. Told before any examination:
-- reduced by 80% (shortfall of $1,000 or more) to 200. Hidden: increased by 20% to 1,200. (Formula of s 284-85(2) INFERRED.)
-- A reckless statement with no shortfall: 40 penalty units = 13,200.
#ASSERT `What is my base penalty amount` `a failure to take reasonable care` 4000 330 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `What is my base penalty amount` `recklessness as to a taxation law` 0 330 EQUALS 13200

#ASSERT `What penalty must I pay for my statement` 1000 4000 `Jake tells the Commissioner before any examination` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `What penalty must I pay for my statement` 1000 4000 `Jake hides the shortfall` EQUALS 1200

§ `ss 286-75, 286-80`

-- k043 variant: a return due 31 October 2029 lodged 1 December 2029 is 31 days late: 2 periods, 2 x 330 = 660. A year late:
-- capped at 5 penalty units, 1,650.
#ASSERT `What penalty must I pay for lodging late` (Date 31 10 2029) (Date 1 12 2029) `small` FALSE 330 EQUALS 660
#ASSERT `What penalty must I pay for lodging late` (Date 31 10 2029) (Date 31 10 2030) `small` FALSE 330 EQUALS 1650

§ `s 298-20`

-- 700 left after a refused remission is more than 2 penalty units (660): Jake may object.
#ASSERT `May I object to the refusal to remit` TRUE 700 330

§ `s 426-105`

-- d072: the Rossi Foundation's trustee is a company that has agreed to the guidelines: a private ancillary fund. d091: the
-- trustee company passing to Daniel's children changes none of the three conditions; had the children replaced the company with
-- themselves as individual trustees (d091 variant), it would stop being one.
#ASSERT `Is my foundation a private ancillary fund` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation a private ancillary fund` FALSE TRUE FALSE

§ `s 426-120`

-- d072: Daniel, aware of the holding out, with no defence, is liable when the trustee company cannot pay. d091: Anjali, unaware
-- and not reasonably expected to be aware, is not.
#ASSERT `Am I liable as a director of the trustee` `d072: Daniel, a director, knew the Foundation was held out as a DGR after its endorsement lapsed`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I liable as a director of the trustee` `d091: Anjali, a new director, could not have known of the holding out`

